    {
      "index": 2,
      "text": "Gate In Procedures",
      "embeds": [],
      "links": []
    },
    {
      "index": 3,
      "text": "At the origin terminal, all Loading Units undergo an inspection before entry into the rail terminal area.\n\nDuring Gate In, SDG Railway staff and the Terminal Operator verify:\n\nDocumentation accuracy (booking reference, consignment note, and dangerous goods declaration if applicable).\n\nCondition and identification of the Loading Unit (container, swap body, or trailer).\n\nCompliance with safety and weight standards prior to train allocation.\n\nOnce verified, the unit is registered in SDG Railway’s digital system and assigned to a railcar for loading.\n\nThe timestamp of Gate In marks the start of operational responsibility under SDG Railway’s custody.",
      "embeds": [],
      "links": []
    },
    {
      "index": 4,
      "text": "",
      "embeds": [],
      "links": []
    },
    {
      "index": 5,
      "text": "Gate Out Procedures",
      "embeds": [],
      "links": []
    },
    {
      "index": 6,
      "text": "At the destination terminal, Loading Units are unloaded and inspected prior to release.\n\nDuring Gate Out, the Terminal Operator and customer representative confirm:\n\nIntegrity and sealing of the unit.\n\nAbsence of visible damage or irregularities.\n\nDelivery documentation signed and validated (Interchange report or electronic acknowledgment).\n\nThe Gate Out timestamp concludes the responsibility of SDG Railway for that shipment.",
      "embeds": [],
      "links": []
    },
    {
      "index": 7,
      "text": "",
      "embeds": [],
      "links": []
    },
